{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-115901",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4(-8)y.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-8.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
